-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Warrant</surname><given-names>E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Nilsson</surname><given-names>D.E.</given-names></name></person-group><source>Invertebrate vision</source><year>2006</year><publisher-name>Cambridge University Press</publisher-name><publisher-loc>Cambridge, UK</publisher-loc><fpage>250</fpage><lpage>290</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kevan</surname><given-names>P.G.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Sun-tracking solar furnaces in high Arctic flowers: significance for pollination and insects</article-title><source>Science</source><volume>189</volume><year>1975</year><fpage>723</fpage><lpage>726</lpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/doi:10.1126/science.189.4204.723">doi:10.1126/science.189.4204.723</ext-link><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17792542</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kevan</surname><given-names>P.G.</given-names></name><name><surname>Chittka</surname><given-names>L.</given-names></name><name><surname>Dyer</surname><given-names>A.G.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Limits to the salience of ultraviolet: lessons from colour vision in bees and birds</article-title><source>J. Exp. Biol</source><volume>204</volume><year>2001</year><fpage>2571</fpage><lpage>2580</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11511673</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kuerten</surname><given-names>L.</given-names></name><name><surname>Schmidt</surname><given-names>U.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The nose pits of the vampire bat <italic>Desmodus rotundus</italic>: sense organs for IR reception</article-title><source>Zeitschrift f